 "sentences_desc": [
  [
   70,
   "**What the envelope cannot explain (mandatory disclosure, registered pre-run).** Sub-band peaks persist with the mechanosensory drive OFF in 11/16 seeds [l154.band], so the envelope accounts for the line's POSITION \u2014 and, with L162's evoked phase lock (carrier median self-PLV .98 on both stored batches, banc/l162/addendum3.json:e_axis; its drive-dependence is recorded in the lane log and is not re-derived here), for its PHASE \u2014 but not for the existence of sub-band power."
  ],
  [
   56,
   "It does NOT license the fast segment as a replacement readout: the registered duty metric is defined on the 0.7-Hz segments, the prior-law expectation for continuous fast drive was structure TOXICITY (the registered B4 degenerate branch, which did not fire here), and a window swapped after the fact is a robustness panel, never a primary result."
  ],
  [
   38,
   "Its dominant non-DC line is bin 6 of a 60-s window = .100 Hz exactly, 1.0 of the envelope's peak amplitude and a local maximum against its neighbours \u2014 the same frequency as the measured slow line [l171.envelope]."
  ],
  [
   37,
   "ZERO rollouts: every number below re-scores STORED traces from the batch that first rolled the XOR pair (B26, n = 16 seeds), and the published cells are reproduced EXACTLY before any new window or filter is read."
  ],
  [
   37,
   "The fast-segment re-score is the cleanest read in the whole lineage: the mass-twin arm sits at absolute floor (meanR .000, 0/16) while the carrier-cut arm keeps 12/16, every one of the 16 seeds moving the same way."
  ],
  [
   33,
   "The high-pass re-score is where \"cleaner\" becomes metric-dependent and we report both directions: its mean-duty contrast is SMALLER than published (+.306 vs +.355) while its seed separation is LARGER (\u0394k 14 vs 10)."
  ],
  [
   32,
   "The mechanism is gap ALIGNMENT, not the chop period: the continuous 1.4-Hz segment overrides two of the six possible gaps, leaving four whose centres sit at 7, 16, 47 and 56 s."
  ],
  [
   31,
   "Those four are near-phase-aligned at a 10-s period (vector strength .95) and badly aligned at the 500-on/400-off chop's own 9-s cycle (.17, i.e. .111 Hz is NOT the dominant envelope line)."
  ]
 ]
